      "title": "Trump-Xi-Putin trilateral meet: Nuclear arms, Ukraine war on agenda",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/trump-xi-putin-trilateral-meet-nuclear-arms-ukraine-war-on-agenda-126111900092_1.html",
      "description": "When President Donald Trump meets on Thursday with China's Xi Jinping and Russia's Vladimir Putin, it could mark a pivot in world history -- or become a quickly forgotten photo op.\nTrump, who will test his reputation as an expert dealmaker in the trilateral meeting, has promoted his time with Xi and Putin -- two of America's leading rivals -- as a chance to hash out rules for controlling nuclear arms and to start resolving the wars in Ukraine and Iran. Experts have kept expectations low for major breakthroughs.\nTrump plans to have a separate one-on-one meeting with Xi -- his third substantial meeting with him this year -- right before the trilateral. He also added a separate sit-down with Putin to his schedule, marking the first time that the leaders have held talks since their discussions in Alaska last year that failed to broker a deal to ease Russia's war in Ukraine.\nTrump has frequently boasted of his rapport with Putin, even as relations between the US and Ukraine appear to hav",
